Route pure speculative-decode batches on FlashInfer + static FP8 KV through the
split-KV Triton verifier on SM80.

This patch is opt-in with VLLM_FP8_SPEC_VERIFY=1 and depends on:

  spec-decode-attn.patch
  spec-decode-int8-kv.patch
  spec-decode-fp8-kv-sm80.patch

Normal FlashInfer prefill and single-token decode are unchanged. The opt-in
builder threshold classifies multi-query speculative verification as decode
metadata on SM80; the runtime hook then fires only for a pure causal decode
batch where a request has more than one query, the KV cache is FP8, there is no
sliding window/softcap/alibi/sink, DCP is off, and the cache layout is NHD.

The common query-start, sequence-length and block-table tensors are retained in
FlashInferMetadata solely for this verifier. They are GPU tensors already owned
by the model runner; no new per-step allocation is introduced.

Apply with experimental/cmp170hx-mixed-fp8/install.sh after the kernel patch.

Written against vLLM 0.27.1.

